# Nubia Red Magic 11S Pro+ (NX809J) U-Boot environment.
#
# The panel is the ONLY console on this board: no UART pads, no USB gadget in
# this build. stdout/stderr go to the video console, which draws into the
# splash buffer ABL left the DPU scanning (0xfc800000, 0x2b00000 bytes), so it
# works with no display driver at all. stdin keeps the always-registered
# "serial" stdio stub so console setup has an input device; it never produces
# input, which is why bootcmd is a self-contained script rather than something
# you interact with.
#
# NOTE the shell is the SIMPLE parser, not hush (CONFIG_HUSH_PARSER is off, and
# so are CMD_TEST/CMD_LS/CMD_FAT): no `if`, no `test`, no `ls`, no `fatls`. A
# bootcmd can only be a linear list, and fallbacks work by letting a failing
# command print its error and fall through to the next one.
stdin=serial
stdout=vidconsole
stderr=vidconsole

# bootdelay is deliberately NOT set: the defconfig compiles in
# CONFIG_BOOTDELAY=-2, which runs bootcmd immediately with no countdown and no
# way to abort. There is nothing to type on anyway.
#
# Load addresses are deliberately NOT set either: mach-snapdragon's
# board_late_init() allocates them at runtime out of ABL's real memory map via
# LMB (honouring /reserved-memory, including the splash carve-out).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What the v2 and v3 runs established, so this does not get re-litigated:
#
#   * boot_b IS reachable and IS correct. v3 found it - "start 0x796d2,
#     size 0x6000, name boot_b" is 24576 x 4096 bytes = 100663296, exactly the
#     96 MiB partition - so the GPT parses and the partition name matches.
#
#   * U-Boot numbers SCSI block devices by AUTO-ASSIGNED devnum
#     (blk_create_devicef(..., -1, ...) in scsi.c), one per detected LUN in LUN
#     order. boot_b's LUN came up as scsi 5, not scsi 4 as the Android sdX
#     numbering suggests, so the partition number must be looked up per device
#     and every device tried - which is what this does.
#
#   * The v3 failure was "FAT sector size mismatch (fs=512, dev=4096)" right
#     before "Error reading config file": the UFS LUNs have a 4096-byte
#     logical block size, mtools had written a 512-byte-sector FAT, and
#     CONFIG_FS_FAT_HANDLE_SECTOR_SIZE_MISMATCH was off - so the driver logged
#     the mismatch and then read as if the sizes matched. Fixed on both sides:
#     the staging FAT is now built with 4096-byte sectors, and the option is
#     enabled so a 512-byte-sector FAT works too.
#
# Order note: sysboot returns only if it failed to boot anything, so the first
# attempt that succeeds ends bootcmd. scsi 5 is tried first because that is
# where boot_b was last seen, and the rest are the fallback chain - the devnum
# assignment can shift if a LUN fails detection on a given boot.
bootcmd=echo; \
echo "=== NX809J: U-Boot -> mainline Linux from the boot_b staging FAT ==="; \
scsi scan; \
echo "--- boot_b partition lookup, per scsi device ---"; \
part number scsi 0 boot_b n0; echo "  scsi0 boot_b=[${n0}]"; \
part number scsi 1 boot_b n1; echo "  scsi1 boot_b=[${n1}]"; \
part number scsi 2 boot_b n2; echo "  scsi2 boot_b=[${n2}]"; \
part number scsi 3 boot_b n3; echo "  scsi3 boot_b=[${n3}]"; \
part number scsi 4 boot_b n4; echo "  scsi4 boot_b=[${n4}]"; \
part number scsi 5 boot_b n5; echo "  scsi5 boot_b=[${n5}]"; \
part number scsi 6 boot_b n6; echo "  scsi6 boot_b=[${n6}]"; \
part number scsi 7 boot_b n7; echo "  scsi7 boot_b=[${n7}]"; \
echo "--- sysboot ---"; \
sysboot scsi 5:${n5} fat ${scriptaddr} /extlinux/extlinux.conf; \
sysboot scsi 4:${n4} fat ${scriptaddr} /extlinux/extlinux.conf; \
sysboot scsi 6:${n6} fat ${scriptaddr} /extlinux/extlinux.conf; \
sysboot scsi 3:${n3} fat ${scriptaddr} /extlinux/extlinux.conf; \
sysboot scsi 7:${n7} fat ${scriptaddr} /extlinux/extlinux.conf; \
sysboot scsi 0:${n0} fat ${scriptaddr} /extlinux/extlinux.conf; \
sysboot scsi 1:${n1} fat ${scriptaddr} /extlinux/extlinux.conf; \
sysboot scsi 2:${n2} fat ${scriptaddr} /extlinux/extlinux.conf; \
echo; \
echo "=== NOTHING BOOTED - the answer is in the lines above. ==="; \
echo "  no scsi device at all            -> the UFS probe itself failed"; \
echo "  FAT sector size mismatch         -> the staging FAT's sector size must be 4096"; \
echo "  boot_b=[..] empty on every line  -> the GPT name is not exactly boot_b"; \
echo "  a sysboot line names a partition -> it read the wrong partition number"
